  "configuration_id": "config_026",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_007 (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the best at 0.639 acc, clearly outperforming transformer aggregation (0.573) and concat fusion (0.619). Multimodal strongly beats RNA-only (0.639 vs 0.519). The main untested lever within the proven avgpool+weighted recipe is the image encoder: upgrading from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L could yield a meaningful accuracy gain since image features are a key multimodal signal. Question: Does a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) push accuracy above 0.639 while keeping the cheap, proven avgpool+weighted pipeline? This is a single-variable extension of the best config, making results interpretable. Cost: ViT-L is ~300M params vs ResNet50's ~25M, so I estimate ~18–25 GPU hours—moderately more expensive than config_007 (10.6) but far cheaper than the concat-fusion configs (~36). With 5 experiments remaining, this is the highest-value exploitation step: it tests the most impactful unexplored axis (image encoder quality) within the already-validated architecture, and a positive result would set up further refinement (e.g., RNA encoder upgrade) in subsequent runs."
}

